<title>AUSTRALIA: Australian bond yields drop,gear up for bengin CPI.</title>
<headline>Australian bond yields drop,gear up for bengin CPI.</headline>
<text>
<p>----------(Snapshot at 9.00 A.M./2300 GMT)------------------</p>
<p>FUTURES					  CASH YIELD</p>
<p>90-DAY BILLS  (JUN) 94.16  (+ 0.05)    6.05    (UNCH)</p>
<p>3-YR T-BONDS  (JUN) 93.30  (+ 0.08)    6.62    (- 0.08)</p>
<p>10-YR T-BONDS (JUN) 92.230 (+0.060)    7.76    (- 0.06)</p>
<p>AUD/USD  0.7761 (PREV 0.7755) US 30-YR  7.04   (- 0.05)</p>
<p>---------------------(April 23)-----------------------------</p>
<p>*Australian bond yields fell to their lowest level since late February as Tuesday's low pay award by the AIRC, benign CPI expectations and rally in U.S. bonds fuelled a month-long rally.</p>
<p>*March quarter CPI due at 11.30 a.m. (0130 GMT).</p>
</text>
